cally seen in Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia (PCD) with Cardiac Anomalies: abnormal axonemal organization of respiratory motile cilia, abnormal sweat electrolytes, decreased fertility, heterotaxy\n\nRelated to Chronic Inflammatory Airway Disease: amnionitis, arthritic joint disease, balanitis\n\nRelated to Congenital Anomaly Syndrome (Cardiac + Respiratory Axis): congenital myasthenic syndrome with tubular aggregates, congenital myasthenic syndromes with glycosylation defect, eyelids malposition disorder\n\nRelated to Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia (PCD) with Cardiac Anomalies: ciliary discoordination due to random ciliary orientation, ciliary dyskinesia with defective radial spokes, ciliary dyskinesia with excessively long cilia\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent lower respiratory tract infections → Congenital Anomaly Syndrome (Cardiac + Respiratory Axis)\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent respiratory infections → Congenital Anomaly Syndrome (Cardiac + Respiratory Axis)\n  A 10-year-old girl is admitted to the medical floor for a respiratory infection → recurrent respiratory infections → Primary Ciliary Dyskinesia (PCD) with Cardiac Anomalies"}
